hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"971","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “I prayed with the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace in Medina, eight, and all seven. I said: Why did he do that? He said: He wanted not to embarrass his nation. He said: While he was staying for a while. Travel, and no fear.” Al-Makhzoumi told us, Sufyan told us something similar. He said: Without fear or travel, and Saeed said: So I said to Ibn Abbas: Why did he do that? He said: He wanted no one from his nation to be embarrassed, and this is how Abdul-Jabbar told us about it once."
"972","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, that Malik told him, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr al-Makki, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the noon and afternoon prayers together, and the sunset and evening prayers together, in other than Fear and no travel.” Malik said: “I think it was raining.” Abu Bakr said: Not all scholars disagreed that combining the two prayers in the city when it is not raining is not permissible, so we know and are certain that Scholars do not agree on the difference that a report from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is authentic in terms of transmission, and there is no contradiction to it from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The scholars of Hijaz disagree that combining the two prayers in the rain is permissible, so we interpreted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, combining them in the presence of the Prophet in the meaning that was not Muslims agree to contradict it, as it is not permissible for Muslims to agree to contradict the report of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, without narrating from the Prophet. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, there is a report that contradicts it. As for what the Iraqis narrated that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gathered a crowd in Medina without fear or rain, It is a mistake and an oversight, and contrary to what all the people of prayer say, even if the report is proven from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he gathered in the presence without fear And no rain. It is not permissible for a Muslim who knows the authenticity of this news to prohibit combining the two prayers in the city without fear or rain. So whoever moves in... He reported this news that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, combined the two prayers without fear, travel, or rain. Then he claimed that combining the two prayers Based on what the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, combined between them, it is not permissible. This is ignorance and oversight and it is not permissible for a scholar to say it."
